Just to add a little to what Andrew wrote:

I can confirm that iwd's AP mode doesn't work with brcmfmac.

I used iwmon to dig a bit deeper into the difference in behaviour =

between hostapd and iwd. The issue is that iwd uses =

NL80211_CMD_REGISTER_FRAME to be notified of incoming management frames, =

and this is what kicks off the 4-Way Handshake in ap.c. But brcmfmac =

does not support this (except in P2P mode?). On the other hand, it seems =

that hostapd reacts to NL80211_CMD_NEW_STATION (which iwd also receives, =

but does nothing with) before starting the authentication. See the =

attached iwmon logs for the difference.

I didn't look it much further, but I hope that helps.

Kind regards,
Alvin

